@startuml 06_standards_hierarchy
title IEC Standards Hierarchy — CIM → ESMP → OpenADR 3.1 / IEC 62746-4

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam packageBorderColor #888888
skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam arrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam noteBorderColor #F9A825

top to bottom direction

package "Abstract Semantic Foundation" <<Frame>> #E8EAF6 {
  class "IEC CIM\n(Common Information Model)" as CIM {
    + Abstract UML ontology
    + Grid assets, market participants,
      time series, measurements
    + Vendor/region neutral
  }
}

package "Regional Contextual Model" <<Frame>> #E8F5E9 {
  class "IEC 62325-351\nESMP\n(European Style Market Profile)" as ESMP {
    + EIC party identification
    + ENTSOE code lists
    + Document header conventions
    + ESMP_DateTimeInterval
    + Time series encoding (explicit / implicit)
  }
}

package "Wholesale Market Operations\n(OUT OF SCOPE for this profile)" <<Frame>> #FFEBEE {
  class "IEC 62325-451-x\nBusiness Process Profiles" as BPP {
    + -451-1: Acknowledgement
    + -451-3: Capacity allocation
    + -451-4: Settlement
    + -451-7: Balancing (TSO–BSP)
  }
}

package "Demand-Side Interface\n(SCOPE of this profile ★)" <<Frame>> #E3F2FD {
  class "IEC 62746-4\nDemand Side Resource Interface" as DSRI {
    + ReferenceEnergyCurveOperatingEnvelope
    + ReferenceEnergyCurveBaselineNotification
    + ReferenceEnergyCurveFlexOffer
    + MarketDERInstruction
    + CommodityPriceExchange
    + MarketDER (registration, TBD)
    Information model layer
  }

  class "OpenADR 3.1\n(IEC/PAS 62746-10-1 candidate)" as OA {
    + REST/JSON/MQTT transport
    + program / event / report / interval
    + OAuth2 authentication
    + Publish-subscribe / webhook
    Transport + API layer
  }
}

CIM  -down-|>  ESMP       : «derives»
ESMP -down-|>  BPP        : «derives»
ESMP -down-|>  DSRI       : «derives»
DSRI -right->  OA         : «semantic alignment\n(this profile)»

note right of OA
  IEC 62746-4 = information model
  (data structures, message semantics,
  CIM UML profiles)

  OpenADR 3.1 = transport + API layer
  (REST/JSON/MQTT, pub-sub, webhooks)

  This profile documents the semantic
  equivalence between the two layers.
end note

note right of BPP
  IEC 62325-451-7 governs TSO–BSP
  wholesale balancing communications.
  Architecturally upstream of OpenADR 3.1.
  Out of scope — but triggers the Aggregator
  who then dispatches via OpenADR.
end note

@enduml
